From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:26:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: isp: set up the J604's IMX958 as macOS
 does

macOS's appleh16camerad sets the IMX958's lens shading target to 84
percent and computes the setfile's noise reduction radial gains from its
lens shading table before it loads the setfile. The J604 carries the same
IMX958, in the same 14-inch camera module as the J714c, so do both on
T8132 too.

In a dim room the J604 delivered about half the brightness macOS shows,
with heavy grain (frame-to-frame difference about 20 of 255 at a mean
level of 28). The radial gains cut the grain most at the edges, where the
shading gain is highest.

The face-detection scene metering setup stays off on T8132: on the T8140
firmware it faults, and it has not run on this one yet.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.c
index 1c1a332f68..d048448492 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.c
@@ -1248,6 +1248,9 @@ static const struct apple_isp_hw apple_isp_hw_t8132 = {
 	.deferred_start = true,
 	.meta_exposure = true,
 	.imx958_wide_cfg6 = true,
+	/* As macOS sets up this camera's IMX958 (appleh16camerad) */
+	.setfile_radial_gain = true,
+	.lsc_ideal_percent = 84,
 };
 
